      "id": "be-s8-cost-functions-c1",
      "heading": "The cubic cost function and its marginal cost",
      "explanation_md": "A cubic cost function: **C(Q) = f + aQ + bQ² + cQ³**. The constant **f** is the fixed cost; everything with Q in it is variable cost.\n\n**Marginal cost** is the derivative: **MC(Q) = a + 2bQ + 3cQ²**. Bring each power down and lower it by one; the constant f disappears because it does not change with output.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "C(Q) = f + aQ + bQ² + cQ³ gives MC(Q) = a + 2bQ + 3cQ² (dC/dQ).",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
